  "description": "The Service Allocator (name\u202f=\u202fServiceAllocator) has recorded a new service allocation event (type\u202f=\u202fEiffelServiceAllocatedEvent, version\u202f=\u202f1.0.0) with identifier **a3f1c2d4-5b6e-3a89-9b0c-2d3e4f5a6b7c** at timestamp **1718501234567** (UTC). The event carries the tags **service** and **allocation** and originates from the source domain **com.example.domain**, host **service-host.example.com**, URI **urn:example:service-allocator**. The serializer in use is **com.example:service-allocator:2.3.1**. Security metadata records the author identity **alice@example.com** and the encrypted digest **d2d2d2d2d2d2d2d2d2d2d2d2d2d2d2d2**.\n\nThe allocated service instance is **svc-12345**, owned by **team\u2011alpha**, and can be accessed at **https://services.example.com/instances/svc-12345**. Attached custom data includes: environment\u202f=\u202fproduction; replicas\u202f=\u202f3; config\u202f=\u202f{cpu:\u202f2vCPU, memory:\u202f4GB}.\n\nThis allocation is linked as a **CAUSE** to the preceding event with identifier **b4e2f3a5-6c7d-3e9f-9a1b-2c3d4e5f6a7b**.",
